  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8e2e2318533cdee478cc197dc2db33bc, type: 3}
  m_Name: Cole'sSpendingProblem
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  displayImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 23e13442c43dad74e89e6168f192b950, type: 3}
  displayText: 'Cole has just sold his company. Now he spend his earnings stupidly.
    In order: <br> He spends 2/3 on a house.<br> He spends 3/4 of his remaining earnings
    on a fast car.<br> He spends 4/5 of his remaining earnings on a gourmet coffee
    machine.<br> He ends with $11,000.<br> How much money did he sell his company
    for?'
  solutionImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 23e13442c43dad74e89e6168f192b950, type: 3}
  solutionText: Solve in reverse order of the spending.<br>Note that 11,000 is equal
    to 1/5 of what he had before spending 4/5ths. <br> 11,000 * 5/1 * 4/1 * 3/1 =
    660,000
